//
// Phase J7b operator gate: ffn_accum, the compiler-formed accumulator ring.
//
// The FFN down-projection written as the naive K loop -- fetch C, in-place
// accumulate (ffn_matmul_bf16_bf16_up_proj), store C, every K step -- which
// air-hoist-dma-in-accum-pattern collapses so the partial sums stay
// L1-resident across K. A and B ride one memtile feed channel per core and
// the C pair rides the shim, which is what keeps every stream circuit-routed
// (see builders/ffn_accum.py for the two measured walls behind that shape).
//
// Three arms, because the phase's claim has three parts that no single check
// can see at once:
//
// 1. STRUCTURE, first because it is host-only and fails fast: the K loop's
//    data movement must drop 4 -> 2 under the hoist pass (the C pair leaves,
//    A and B stay) and the channel-lowered module must carry ZERO
//    packet-typed channels. A ring that failed to form computes identical
//    numbers one DDR round trip per K step slower, invisible below.
// 2. NUMBERS, on real NPU2: opcheck.py against the FP32 reference at the
//    registry GEMM scale, np.isclose over the full output at rtol=1.6e-2,
//    zero permitted mismatches.
// 3. The NEGATIVE CONTROL: one element of the packed a perturbed after the
//    reference is computed, and the comparison itself must reject the run.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down: XRTRunner.run_test holds
// /tmp/npu.lock across load and dispatch, interlocking with every other NPU
// job here. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here instead would
// DEADLOCK against the gate command that invokes this suite.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_ffn_accum_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_ffn_accum_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-ffn-accum-structure | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STRUCT
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-ffn-accum PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-ffn-accum-fault PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FAULT
//
// The hoist count and the packet count are stated inside the verdict line, so
// a lowering that kept the C pair in the loop -- or found packet channels --
// cannot match here; the script itself fails vacuous zeros (no unlowered
// DMAs, feed channel present by name).
// STRUCT: [ffn-accum-structure] ffn_accum [64x3072x768]: PASS (K-loop 4 -> 2, 0 packet-typed
// STRUCT: [ffn-accum-structure] PASS
//
// Both lines, not just the verdict: the first is XRTRunner's own, the second
// names the operator and shape, so a test wired to the wrong operator fails
// here rather than passing quietly.
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] ffn_accum [64x3072x768]: PASS
//
// The injection line first: it names the element and both values. Flat index
// (0,) of the packed a is element (0, 0) under any packing, so the control
// does not depend on the packing arithmetic it guards.
// FAULT: [fault-inject] input 0 at (0,)
// FAULT: [opcheck] ffn_accum [64x3072x768]: FAIL
// FAULT: NEGATIVE CONTROL: PASS
